  "result": "`formatDuration` is added and committed, but the commit title ends in a placeholder id.\n\n- **Function:** `src/core/duration.ts` renders `3_723_000` as `1h 2m 3s`. It drops zero leading units, so `123_000` gives `2m 3s`. It keeps zero inner units, so `3_603_000` gives `1h 0m 3s`. Sub-second, zero and negative inputs give `0s`.\n- **Tests:** `test/core/duration.test.ts` covers those cases. I also added its weight to `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`.\n- **Checks:** `npm run fast` passed with Biome, boundaries, tsc and the related tests.\n- **Helpers:** I found nothing in `src/` to reuse. The only candidate was a `padStart` helper in `src/worker/`. Core may only import its own files, so I wrote it self-contained.\n- **Commit:** `e5239e0` is titled \"Add formatDuration to core (t-unknown)\". My brief had no task id, and the repo convention puts the id at the end of the title. Give me the real id and I'll amend the title.",
